<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70386" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεοσσός</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεοττ-</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>young bird, nestling, chick,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.311
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.323
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				425
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				835
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				2.24
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπτῆνες ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.48a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>any young animal,</i> as a young crocodile, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.68
			</span></i>; of young children, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				256
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				501
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				403
			</span></i> (lyr.), al., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				776a
			</span></i>: fem., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦν νεοττὸς καὶ
			νέα</span> (sc. Lais) <i><span class="en">
				Epicr.
				3.15
			</span></i>: in pl., <i>young bees,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				7.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				624a22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄρεως ν.,</span> of the cock,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				835
			</span></i> (also ironically, of a person, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				104
			</span></i>): collective, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππου ν.</span> the
			horse's <i>brood,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				825
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>yolk</i> of an egg, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				565a3
			</span></i>, Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.344
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεοττίον.</span>—The disyll. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοσσός</span></b>  is cited in <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				109
			</span></i> from <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				113
			</span></i> and occurs in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				2081
			</span></i> (<i>b) Fr.</i><i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>: this and cogn. forms (commonly found in later Gr.) are
			condemned as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδόκιμα</span> by <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				182
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
